    "turn_text": "Yeah, I'll try to do this one quickly. I probably went to law school in part because I didn't know exactly what I wanted to do. And everyone says, a law degree is a great degree to have. When I talk to people now and give students advice, I always remind them that no one finishes the sentence. A law degree is a great degree to have to practice law. really what they equipped you to do when you leave law schools go practice law. So I went, when I first out of law school, I went to the really kind of big regional firm. My grandfather's firm is a small firm, a small law firm, and went there, and then went from there to the attorney general's office, which really more satisfied, I think, my itch for policy and helping people without knowing that when I went to law school. But I was not planning on running for office. I was practicing law. My wife was working for young brands at the time. And we got pregnant. We had twins. And we had one of those stories where we went for the 24-week checkup. They said, everything looks so good. Don't come back for another month. The next day, my wife called me from work. She's laughing. She goes, I could believe this. I just peed my pants. The next call I got, she's in the emergency room. Her water broken. 24 weeks. I need",
