    "turn_text": "not trying to open up another location. He's not trying to do something else. But I think of an entrepreneur, right? I think of that person who is pushing that boundary, who is taking those risks, who is trying to make something else. It's not that one is good and one is bad. They're both great. But it is a different, sometimes it can be a different personality, sometimes it can be a different skill set. You know, even I've dealt with entrepreneurs, both in my legal career and in policy, you get an entrepreneur, you might be able to start a business, and that's a skill set. But then you can't take it past a certain point. And then there's people who could take a business from a small business to a medium-sized business, and that's their skill set. But they don't want to do anything else. And there's people who can even say, okay, look, you're a medium-sized business. My skill set is making you a large business, right? There's all sorts of different skill sets, but I think it's good to talk about both of them. And when we talk about innovation, I think when we talk about innovation, we've got to talk about how to create more entrepreneurs. That is a pathway to the American dream that honestly is open to anyone. That it's so important to say that again, the entrepreneurship, the pathway to the American dream that is open to anyone. There is no educational barrier to entry. There is no, at least in theory, there is no other bear to entry, whether it's sexism, racism, any other type of, it's just if you have a good idea and you can work hard, you can achieve that American dream. We have to help that make that a reality. I think we have to recognize a few things that have kept people from being entrepreneurs. One, I think we have to see something I hear about all the time. In Louisville, we hear about it in the committee, we hear about it from across the country that is access to capital. So if you are starting with nothing, it is much harder to go after those dreams. If you don't have something to fall back on, you can't get the capital you need to start your",
