    "turn_text": "that's why I love what you're doing on this committee and what Vice President Harris is talking about because some kind of way, and it's like a dog whistle for me. It's like, oh my God, these people understand, these elected officials understand that the way to success in the United States is through business. And I'm telling you, it's changing. And I love that. You are working hard, not only to try to get people money, you know, capital loans, something that I'm not as interested in as getting a government contract, for example, for my business. But I love that you're saying, look, there's a whole bunch of things we could be doing to help. And vice president Harris recognized it because she has friends. I know vice president Harris has friends that have businesses off their kitchen table. She saw it in college. She saw her whole life. She saw the struggle. She sees what's going on. And I don't know that we've ever had a president that really has seen that or gotten that to the extent that she has. And I'm sorry, but people that have even a side hustle, we outnumber. We outnumber people that work for corporations. I mean, we are a large voting black. And so, you know, it's real, like what we can do and what we can bring the table. And, you know, if we can get in and have conversations with people like you, which is what I'm having right now, we can come and bring innovation and ideas and thought leadership to the process, you know? And it's not just like going to a town hall and talking to small businesses and, you know, we're bringing them in on a virtual call with the SBA. It's like, literally, if you've got people finally that get in, to our government and understand what we're talking about and what problems we're really having. I know change is going to come for us. I have no doubt in my mind about it. And you're an optimist.",
